# Form Wrappers (`etoro-ui/form`)

RHF-enabled wrappers that connect React Hook Form field state to UI controls.
underlying `etoro-ui` dumb controls (`EtInput`, `EtCheckbox`, `EtRadioGroup`, `EtChip`, `EtToggleSwitch`, etc.).

Import everything from the dedicated sub-path:

```tsx
import { useForm, FormField, EtFormInput, EtFormCheckbox, EtFormRadioGroup, EtFormErrorMessage } from 'etoro-ui/form';
```

---

## `FormField` — Generic Form Field (Recommended)

Works with **any** controlled component via a render callback. No per-component wrapper needed.

```tsx
import { FormField, useForm } from 'etoro-ui/form';
```

### Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `name` | `FieldPath<T>` | required | RHF field name (supports dotted paths) |
| `control` | `Control<T>` | required | RHF control from `useForm()` |
| `rules` | `RegisterOptions` | - | RHF validation rules (or use a resolver on `useForm`) |
| `children` | `(field, error) => ReactNode` | required | Render callback |
| `showError` | `boolean` | `true` | Auto-render error text below children |
| `renderError` | `(error: FieldError) => ReactNode` | - | Custom error renderer |
| `style` | `StyleProp<ViewStyle>` | - | Style on the wrapper View |

### Basic — text input

```tsx
<FormField name="email" control={control} rules={{ required: 'Email is required' }}>
  {(field) => (
    <EtInput defaultValue={field.value} variant="contained">
      <EtInput.Label>Email</EtInput.Label>
      <EtInput.Field onChangeText={field.onChange} />
    </EtInput>
  )}
</FormField>
```

### Country selector

```tsx
<FormField name="countryId" control={control}>
  {(field) => (
    <CountrySelect
      label="Country"
      selectedCountryId={field.value}
      onCountrySelected={(country) => field.onChange(country.countryId)}
      variant="available"
    />
  )}
</FormField>
```

### Checkbox

```tsx
<FormField name="terms" control={control} rules={{ validate: v => v || 'Required' }} showError={false}>
  {(field, error) => (
    <EtCheckbox value={error && !field.value ? 'error' : field.value} onChange={field.onChange}>
      <EtCheckbox.Label>I accept the terms</EtCheckbox.Label>
    </EtCheckbox>
  )}
</FormField>
```

### Custom error renderer

```tsx
<FormField
  name="email"
  control={control}
  renderError={(err) => <CustomErrorBanner message={err.message} />}
>
  {(field) => <EtInput defaultValue={field.value}>...</EtInput>}
</FormField>
import {
  useForm, FormProvider,
  EtFormInput, EtFormCheckbox, EtFormRadio, EtFormRadioGroup,
  EtFormChip, EtFormChipGroup,
  EtFormToggleSwitch, EtFormToggleSwitchGroup,
  EtFormErrorMessage
} from 'etoro-ui/form';
```

### No auto error (handle via `error` arg)

```tsx
<FormField name="country" control={control} showError={false}>
  {(field, error) => (
    <CountrySelect
      label={error ? 'Country (required)' : 'Country'}
      selectedCountryId={field.value}
      onCountrySelected={(c) => field.onChange(c.countryId)}
    />
  )}
</FormField>
```

### With BFF validation resolver (no `rules` needed)

Use `bffValidationResolver` at the `useForm` level instead of per-field `rules`:

```tsx
import { bffValidationResolver } from '@etoro/features/onboarding/kyc/core/utils';

const FIELD_MAP = {
  address: 'addressInfo.address',
  city: 'addressInfo.city',
  countryId: 'addressInfo.countryId',
};

const resolver = useMemo(
  () => bffValidationResolver(resolvedData?.validation, FIELD_MAP, t),
  [resolvedData?.validation, t],
);

const form = useForm({ defaultValues, resolver, mode: 'onChange' });

// No rules needed — BFF drives validation:
<FormField name="address" control={form.control}>
  {(field) => <EtInput defaultValue={field.value}>...</EtInput>}
</FormField>
```

### When to use `FormField` vs component-specific wrappers

| Use `FormField` when | Use `EtFormInput`/`EtFormCheckbox` when |
|---|---|
| Custom components (CountrySelect, tile groups) | Standard EtInput text fields with full context bypass |
| Any third-party or feature-level component | You need `EtFormInput.Field` auto-binding (ref, onBlur) |
| Rapid prototyping / new screens | Existing code already uses the compound wrapper |

