## Compound Wrappers (component-specific)

### Single-Value Wrappers
- `EtFormInput` - Text input fields
- `EtFormCheckbox` - Boolean checkbox
- `EtFormRadio` - Boolean radio indicator (display-only)
- `EtFormRadioGroup` - Single-select radio group
- `EtFormChip` - Boolean chip selection
- `EtFormToggleSwitch` - Boolean toggle switch

### Multi-Select Group Wrappers (string[] fields)
- `EtFormChipGroup` - Multi-select chip group
- `EtFormToggleSwitchGroup` - Multi-select toggle switches

### Shared Error Display
- `EtFormErrorMessage` - Aggregates errors from multiple fields

---

### `EtFormInput`

Wraps `EtInput` for text input. Binds `useController` via context.

**Sub-components:**

| Sub-component | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `EtFormInput` (root) | Calls `useController`, provides context. Required: `name`, `control`. Optional: `rules`, `hideError` |
| `EtFormInput.Control` | Renders `EtInput` shell with error injected from context |
| `EtFormInput.Label` | Re-export of `EtInput.Label` |
| `EtFormInput.Field` | Text input auto-bound to RHF (`onChangeText`, `onBlur`, `ref`) |
| `EtFormInput.ErrorMessage` | Inline error text. Returns null when no error |
| `EtFormInput.TextAdornment` | Re-export of `EtInput.TextAdornment` |
| `EtFormInput.IconAdornment` | Re-export of `EtInput.IconAdornment` |

**Basic usage (inline error):**

```tsx
const { control } = useForm({ defaultValues: { email: '' }, mode: 'onBlur' });

<EtFormInput
  name="email"
  control={control}
  rules={{ required: 'Email is required' }}
>
  <EtFormInput.Control>
    <EtFormInput.Label required>Email</EtFormInput.Label>
    <EtFormInput.Field placeholder="name@example.com" keyboardType="email-address" />
  </EtFormInput.Control>
  <EtFormInput.ErrorMessage />
</EtFormInput>
```

**External shared error (`hideError`):**

Use `hideError` when the error is displayed via `EtFormErrorMessage` instead of inline:

```tsx
<EtFormInput name="email" control={control} rules={{ required: 'Required' }} hideError>
  <EtFormInput.Control>
    <EtFormInput.Label>Email</EtFormInput.Label>
    <EtFormInput.Field />
  </EtFormInput.Control>
</EtFormInput>
```

**With custom `onChange`/`onBlur` side-effects:**

Both the RHF handler and the custom callback run. RHF always runs first.

```tsx
<EtFormInput.Field
  onChangeText={(text) => console.log('side-effect', text)}
  onBlur={(e) => console.log('blurred')}
/>
```

