### `EtFormToggleSwitchGroup`

Wraps multiple toggle switches for multi-select array fields (manages `string[]` field).

**Sub-components:**

| Sub-component | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `EtFormToggleSwitchGroup` (root) | Calls `useController`, provides context |
| `EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.Control` | Container for toggle switch options |
| `EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.Option` | Individual toggle switch row with label |
| `EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.ErrorMessage` | Inline error text |

**Usage:**

```tsx
<EtFormToggleSwitchGroup
  name="qualifications"
  control={control}
  rules={{ validate: v => v?.length > 0 || 'Select at least one' }}
>
  <EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.Control>
    <EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.Option value="cert">
      Certificate
    </EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.Option>
    <EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.Option value="degree">
      Degree
    </EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.Option>
    <EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.Option value="experience">
      Professional Experience
    </EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.Option>
  </EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.Control>
  <EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.ErrorMessage />
</EtFormToggleSwitchGroup>
```

**Field value:** `string[]` (array of selected values)

**With custom `onPress` override:**

```tsx
<EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.Option
  value="special"
  onPress={() => {
    // Custom behavior (e.g., for "None of these" option)
  }}
>
  None of these apply
</EtFormToggleSwitchGroup.Option>
```

